cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite this repository and its method references.
type: software
license: MIT
license-url: LICENSE
title: Parking Trajectory Planning with H-OBCA and Adaptive Constraint Generation
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Yuwen
    affiliation: The University of Hong Kong
abstract: >
  A parking planning study using Hybrid A* warm starts, H-OBCA-style
  optimization and independent interval collision verification. The frozen
  128-case backend benchmark compares node-only, fixed-interior and adaptive
  constraint workflows. A separate study diagnoses HA search failures.
keywords:
  - automated parking
  - Hybrid A*
  - optimization-based collision avoidance
  - trajectory verification
